    "content": "Mogadishu, Somalia — Somalia took part in the second Regional Education Conference of the East African Community (EAC), held from August 25 to 28, 2026, in Nairobi, Kenya. The delegation, headed by the Deputy Minister of Education, Culture and Higher Education, joined over 600 participants, including ministers, senior officials, development partners, academics, and representatives from civil society organizations across the region.\n\nThe conference served as a platform for EAC member states to deliberate on pressing education challenges, exchange best practices, and explore strategies to improve learning outcomes. Somalia's participation highlighted its commitment to aligning its education sector with regional standards, particularly as the country continues post-conflict reconstruction and expansion of educational access.\n\nThis year's gathering was a follow-up to an earlier regional dialogue, reflecting ongoing efforts to harmonize education policies among member states. For Somalia, active engagement in such forums is seen as vital for benefiting from shared resources and expertise, especially in areas like teacher training and curriculum development.\n\nFor members of the Somali diaspora, the conference outcomes may influence education initiatives in their home country, as integration into the EAC framework could open doors for scholarships, joint research, and cross-border education partnerships. Observers note that Somalia's presence signals a positive trajectory toward regional cooperation, though significant work remains to ensure tangible benefits reach communities on the ground.\n\nRead the original report from Radio Dalsan here: https://radiodalsan.com/2026/08/29/somalia-participates-in-east-african-education-conference/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=somalia-participates-in-east-african-education-conference",
